  "findings": [
    "P0 removes page-shape garbage and unsupported free answering, but exposes the low live-discovery recall that the old baseline hid.",
    "Balanced restores one WebWalkerQA exact target page and lowers Web P95 in this run, but it does not recover any answerable Web case.",
    "Enhanced raises WebWalkerQA root-domain recall to 80%, but exact-page recall stays at 2.5% and P95 rises to 29.2 seconds.",
    "The Enhanced Web gain is dominated by benchmark root_url seeding and one-hop expansion: 94.49% of its accepted evidence is on the supplied root site. Normal chat does not normally have this root_url oracle.",
    "FRAMES has no root_url scope. Enhanced leaves domain and exact-page recall at zero, raises F1 only from 1.23% to 1.53%, and increases P95 from 25.8 to 27.3 seconds versus Balanced.",
    "Enhanced answered 14 Web cases, but Web F1 is only 6.43% and exact-page recall is unchanged; generic page support is not equivalent to answering the requested historical fact.",
    "No profile is production-ready. Keep P0 evidence admission, do not enable Enhanced globally, and optimize exact target-page discovery before relaxing abstention."
  ],
  "comparison_limitations": [
    "A and B are frozen historical live runs; C and D are new sequential live Bing runs, so upstream result fluctuation is not controlled across all four arms.",
    "A predates the exact_page_recall metric; its 2.5% value was recomputed from normalized gold and evidence URLs.",
    "Supported-claim rate only checks whether generated claims are supported by selected evidence; it does not establish that the evidence answers the benchmark question.",
    "WebWalkerQA supplies root_url to the scoped Agent. The Enhanced root seed is therefore useful for bounded site walking but should not be interpreted as general Web search recall."
  ]
}
